"description": "WCAG 2.1 contrast audit with the maths baked in: for each foreground/background pair the renderer computes the relative luminance and contrast ratio, shows a live sample swatch, and badges AA (4.5:1), AA large (3:1) and AAA (7:1) as pass or fail. Failing pairs get the nearest passing colour, found by mixing the foreground toward black or white in 5% steps until it clears AA. A summary line counts the passes. For an agent composing a surface this is the difference between \"looks fine\" and \"is readable\". No JavaScript; light or dark.",
